Y. Yang, D. Cer, A. Ahmad, M. Guo, J. Law, N. Constant, G. H. Abrego, S. Yuan, C. Tar, Y.-h. Sung, <em id="bib.bib26.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">et al.</em>, “Multilingual universal sentence encoder for semantic retrieval,” in <em id="bib.bib26.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: System Demonstrations</em>, 2020.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A0.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">-A</span> </span><span id="A0.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Method Details</span></h3>

<section id="A0.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A0.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">-A</span>1 </span>Annotation</h4>

<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To generate structured reasoning annotations, we employ the video understanding capabilities of Gemini-2.5-Pro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>. Our process begins with the LeRobot-formatted LIBERO-10<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/physical-intelligence/libero" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/physical-intelligence/libero</a></span></span></span> and LIBERO-90<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/jesbu1/libero_90_lerobot/tree/main" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/jesbu1/libero_90_lerobot/tree/main</a></span></span></span> demonstration datasets. These have been pre-filtered to exclude unsuccessful trajectories and contain agentview image observations corrected via the script provided by the OpenVLA authors.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each demonstration episode, we compile the agentview images into a 10 fps video. We then prompt Gemini-2.5-Pro with the task instruction, the corresponding video, and the prompt template shown in Figure <a href="#A0.F7" title="Fig. 7 ‣ -A1 Annotation ‣ -A Method Details ‣ Do What You Say: Steering Vision-Language-Action Models via Runtime Reasoning-Action Alignment Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. The model’s task is to generate a sequence of textual sub-plans and identify the concluding timestep for each one.</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This output is then structured into the following format to serve as the intermediate reasoning signal for our model:</p>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A0.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A0.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Plans</span>: &lt;all text plans in the task&gt;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What has been done</span>: &lt;completed plans&gt;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A0.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A0.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Now I need to do</span>: &lt;the next text plan to execute&gt;</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since the end of one sub-plan marks the beginning of the next, we use the generated timesteps to align and supervise the model’s reasoning generation at the start of each new action sequence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.16281v1/annotation_prompt.svg" id="A0.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 7</span>: </span><span id="A0.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt Template for Reasoning Annotations</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A0.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="A0.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">-A</span>2 </span>Training</h4>

<div id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the recipe in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> to train our base reasoning VLA model <math id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝝅</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;">-reason</span>. The hyperparameters used for training are listed in Table <a href="#A0.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ -A2 Training ‣ -A Method Details ‣ Do What You Say: Steering Vision-Language-Action Models via Runtime Reasoning-Action Alignment Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>. The training of <math id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝝅</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;">-reason</span> takes around 20 hours on 8 A100 GPU or 10 hours on 8 H100 GPU. For our baseline <math id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#B08CF0;" mathcolor="#B08CF0">𝝅</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#B08CF0;" mathcolor="#B08CF0">𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the same hyperparameters used for LIBERO finetuning from openpi repository<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi</a></span></span></span>. For learning the Q function in <math id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#C979E6;" mathcolor="#C979E6">𝝅</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#C979E6;" mathcolor="#C979E6">𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#C979E6;">-V-GPS</span>, we use the original code from the paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> and select Implicit Q Learning (IQL) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> algorithm to learn the Q function from offline demonstration dataset LIBERO-100.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A0.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE I</span>: </span><span id="A0.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters<span id="A0.T1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. The Hyperparameters we use to train and evaluate <math id="A0.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\pi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝝅</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;" mathcolor="#646464">𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\pi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A0.T1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#646464;">-reason</span>.</span></span></figcaption>
<p id="A0.T1.7" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A0.T1.7.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:251.3pt;height:133.2pt;vertical-align:-64.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">

<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Hyperparameter</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Value</span></span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Training Batch Size</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">128</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Validation Batch Size</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">64</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Training Steps</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">30000</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Max Token Length</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">415</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Text Loss Coefficient</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">0.5</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Action Loss Coefficient</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">0.5</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Image Size</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><math id="A0.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(224,224,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>224,224</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(224,224,3)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Prediction Horizon</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">16</span></span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">Action Horizon</span>
<span id="A0.T1.7.1.1.1.1.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">5</span></span>
